# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# This is a cookie file for Facebook authentication
# To create this file:
# 1. Install a browser extension like "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" (Chrome/Edge) or "cookies.txt" (Firefox)
# 2. Log into Facebook in your browser
# 3. Export cookies for facebook.com
# 4. Save the exported file as "facebook_cookies.txt" in the bot directory
# 5. Remove this .example file

# Example format (replace with your actual cookie data):
# .facebook.com	TRUE	/	FALSE	1735689600	c_user	your_user_id_here
# .facebook.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1735689600	xs	your_session_token_here
# .facebook.com	TRUE	/	FALSE	1735689600	datr	your_browser_token_here

# Benefits of using Facebook cookies:
# - Access to most Facebook content (photos, videos)
# - Bypass anti-bot detection
# - Access to private/friends-only content (if you have access)
# - Better success rate for media downloads

# Important Notes:
# - Facebook has strict anti-scraping measures
# - Cookies expire and need to be refreshed regularly
# - Success rates may vary due to Facebook's changing policies
# - Consider using a dedicated Facebook account for bot access

# If downloads start failing, try:
# 1. Exporting fresh cookies
# 2. Using a different Facebook account
# 3. Clearing browser cache before exporting cookies